summary.value:
This paper introduces Common Pile v0.1, an 8TB openly licensed dataset for LLM pre-training, covering 30 diverse sources. To demonstrate its utility, the authors train Comma v0.1, a 7B-parameter model on 1T tokens from the dataset. Despite using only open data, Comma achieves performance competitive with models like LLaMA 7B, especially on knowledge and code benchmarks.

The authors contribute:
1. A publicly released, large-scale, open-license dataset for LLM pretraining;
2. A high-performance model trained on this dataset, demonstrating the viability of ethical and transparent model development;
3. A reproducible pipeline including source selection, data filtering, mixing heuristics, tokenizer training, and model checkpoints.

